# Family A1/A10: lane queue kinds (internal/queue). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/queue
BENCH=BenchmarkMemory/Queue
REF=mutexring
AUTO_KEY=queue
ADR=14
TITLE="Memory lane queue kinds (A1), with unsafe slot addressing (A10)"
# The unsafe slot addressing (A10) has its own declaration,
# hack/bakeoff/A10.env, so that its numbers land in a scorecard of their own
# rather than overwriting this one. It measures this same package and root
# under -tags iqmq_unsafe; ADR-021 compares the two scorecards kind by kind.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="ns/op & p99 under MPMC contention, 0 allocs -> seq-MPMC expected; mutex ring retained as 'Safe'"
# MATRIX=full because the smoke grid measures none of the three things the
# criterion names. It produces P=1,4 / batch=1,16 / occupancy=50, so there is
# no MPMC contention point, no near-full row and no near-empty row -- and the
# stopped campaign measured exactly that for family A1 before anything
# noticed. `full` is now the criterion's own grid rather than §9.1's whole
# benchmark column: P{1,32} x batch{1,256} x occupancy{0,95} over the four
# modes, 226 rows, plus the /latency arm that reports the p99. The column's
# full cross is `huge` (894 rows, 9.7 h per build against 2.5 h); the middle P
# rungs duplicate a contention axis the harness sweeps on every row
# (-cpu=1,4,8,32) and occupancy=50 is a point no criterion reads. Assumptions
# A24.61 and A24.62.
MATRIX=full
DECIDED_AT="MPMC P=1 P=32 batch=1 batch=256 occupancy=0 occupancy=95 latency"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op p99-ns"
# `spsc` and `mpsc` cannot run the multi-producer and multi-consumer shapes
# at all -- queue.Kind.Modes says so -- so of the 106 rows the old grid
# produced, the intersection across all nine kinds was two SPSC rows, and a
# single-producer queue would have won the family and been bound as the
# engine's default MPMC lane queue. Declaring them here takes them out of the
# comparable set instead of letting the intersection discover them, and
# `make bench-lint` fails if a kind that is not declared here turns out to be
# narrower than the rest. They are still measured, still scored on the rows
# they have, and ADR-014 reports them as the specialisations they are.
PARTIAL_KINDS="spsc=single producer and single consumer by construction (queue.Kind.Modes = ModeSPSC); mpsc=single consumer by construction (queue.Kind.Modes = ModeSPSC|ModeMPSC), so no SPMC or MPMC row"
# A10 is this same package, root and grid compiled with -tags iqmq_unsafe;
# row A10's ">10% gain" is a join of the two scorecards on the row name, so
# the two declarations must stay at the same MATRIX.
SHARES_ROOT="A10"
